<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The app's two shareable directories, and nothing else.

    A FileProvider that was given a broad path - "everything under the app's
    own files" - would let any app that could name our authority read the
    user's downloaded releases or exported boards. These are the two
    subdirectories that are handed to another app on purpose:

    `files-path/updates`
    A downloaded APK. `files-path`, not `cache-path`, and this line is
    load-bearing in a way that is invisible until it is wrong: the cache is the
    one Android is free to empty whenever it likes, and a downloaded APK must
    outlive the trip to Settings where the user grants the install permission -
    so #61 moved these downloads into the app's private files storage. This
    entry did not follow them: the provider was still publishing an empty
    directory under the cache. Nothing reports that at build time.
    `FileProvider.getUriForFile` throws at *runtime*, on the downloaded APK, the
    first time the user presses Install; `openInstaller` swallows the throw and
    reports that nothing opened; and the updater says "This device has no app
    installer" on a phone with a perfectly working package installer. Every
    update on every device failed that way, and the download itself was fine.

    `cache-path/exports`
    A PNG rendered by the tier board's exporter. The opposite trade-off on
    purpose: the file exists for one share-chooser round trip, and the system is
    welcome to evict it afterwards. It is written to `cacheDir/exports`, which is
    exactly what this root publishes. Moving either half without the other fails
    at the same final step - the chooser receives no URI - so the two are one
    contract just as the update pair is.

    `UpdateFileProviderPathsTest` reads this file and compares the update root
    with the directory `UpdateManager` actually writes to, so those two cannot
    drift apart again without a test going red.
-->
<paths>
    <files-path
        name="updates"
        path="updates/" />
    <!--
    An extension APK downloaded by the Extensions tab. The same contract as
    `updates`: the file has to survive the trip to Settings to grant "install
    unknown apps", so it is written to filesDir, not the cache Android may empty
    in between. Without this path the system installer receives no content URI and
    every extension install silently fails after a successful download.
    -->
    <files-path
        name="extensions"
        path="extensions/" />
    <cache-path
        name="exports"
        path="exports/" />
</paths>
